From: AgentK <dmitryk@3vium.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 04:55:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: qmi_wwan: mark the DTR quirk for BroadMobi BM806

Make the DTR requirement explicit for the BroadMobi BM806U/BM806C
(2020:2033) fitted to the D-Link DWR-921 rev C3, matching its BM818
sibling (2020:2060) directly below.

This is a documentation change, not a fix. The part reports bcdUSB 2.01,
so qmi_wwan_bind() already takes the DTR path through its

	dev->driver_info->data & QMI_WWAN_QUIRK_DTR ||
	le16_to_cpu(dev->udev->descriptor.bcdUSB) >= 0x0201

condition regardless of the table entry, and behaviour on this device is
identical with and without this patch -- verified on hardware, with no USB
errors either way. It only changes anything for a BM806 variant that
reports an older bcdUSB.

In particular this does NOT fix the dead-downlink failure seen on the
DWR-921 C3. DTR was already being asserted throughout that failure. The
actual cause was the packet data session being owned by the modem's own
autoconnect rather than by a host WDS client, so the host never held a
packet data handle; that is fixed in userspace, in the qmi proto script.

Signed-off-by: AgentK <dmitryk@3vium.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c
@@ -1333,7 +1333,7 @@ static const struct usb_device_id products
 	{QMI_FIXED_INTF(0x2001, 0x7e35, 4)},	/* D-Link DWM-222 */
 	{QMI_FIXED_INTF(0x2001, 0x7e3d, 4)},	/* D-Link DWM-222 A2 */
 	{QMI_FIXED_INTF(0x2020, 0x2031, 4)},	/* Olicard 600 */
-	{QMI_FIXED_INTF(0x2020, 0x2033, 4)},	/* BroadMobi BM806U */
+	{QMI_QUIRK_SET_DTR(0x2020, 0x2033, 4)},	/* BroadMobi BM806U/BM806C */
 	{QMI_QUIRK_SET_DTR(0x2020, 0x2060, 4)},	/* BroadMobi BM818 */
 	{QMI_FIXED_INTF(0x0f3d, 0x68a2, 8)},    /* Sierra Wireless MC7700 */
 	{QMI_FIXED_INTF(0x114f, 0x68a2, 8)},    /* Sierra Wireless MC7750 */
